  "facts": [
    "Zigana Tunnel, Turkey's longest road tunnel at 14,481 m, opened in 2023, cutting the 8 km zigzag of the Zigana Pass and shaving twenty minutes off the drive.",
    "Built to replace the 1980s Zigana Tunnel, the twin‑tube design bypasses the 2,032‑m Zigana Pass, showcasing modern engineering in the Pontic Mountains.",
    "The tunnel links D.885 (E97) between Torul in Gümüşhane and Maçka in Trabzon, bridging provincial borders with a seamless 14.5‑km passage."
